==================================================================
DAY 59 - PART A: THEORY
CNI Deep Dive: Calico vs Cilium
Time: 40 minutes
==================================================================

1. SIDE BY SIDE
---------------
                     Calico                       Cilium
  Data plane         iptables/nftables, eBPF,     eBPF
                     or Windows HNS
  Routing            BGP (no overlay) or VXLAN/   VXLAN/Geneve overlay
                     IP-in-IP                     or native routing
  kube-proxy         keeps it, or replaces it     can fully replace it
                     in eBPF mode                 (kubeProxyReplacement)
  Policies           K8s NetworkPolicy + Calico   K8s NetworkPolicy +
                     NetworkPolicy /              CiliumNetworkPolicy
                     GlobalNetworkPolicy (order,  (L7: HTTP methods/
                     deny rules, host endpoints)  paths, DNS/FQDN rules)
  Observability      flow logs (more in paid      Hubble: live flows,
                     editions)                    service map, drops
  Extras             BGP peering with physical    Service mesh features,
                     routers, IPAM pools          Cluster Mesh, Gateway
                                                  API, bandwidth mgr
  Seen in            enterprise/on-prem, EKS/AKS  GKE Dataplane V2,
                     policy add-on                AKS (Azure CNI by
                                                  Cilium), EKS options


2. BEYOND STANDARD NETWORKPOLICY
--------------------------------
Standard NetworkPolicy: L3/L4 (IPs, ports), allow-only, namespaced.
Extensions add:
  - explicit DENY rules and rule ORDER (Calico)
  - CLUSTER-WIDE policies (Calico GlobalNetworkPolicy,
    CiliumClusterwideNetworkPolicy)
  - L7: "only GET /api/*" (Cilium)
  - DNS-based egress: "only to *.amazonaws.com" (Cilium toFQDNs,
    Calico Enterprise)
(The upstream "AdminNetworkPolicy" API aims to standardise cluster-
wide/admin policies.)


3. WHEN TO CHOOSE WHICH
-----------------------
Calico: you need BGP with your data-centre network, mixed Windows
nodes, or a proven simple iptables setup.
Cilium: large scale, eBPF performance, L7 policies, deep visibility
with Hubble, kube-proxy replacement.
Both are excellent; most cloud providers now offer one of them.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- Both enforce NetworkPolicy; extensions differ.
- Cilium = eBPF + Hubble + L7; Calico = flexible routing (BGP) +
  ordered/global policies.
